1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too.

3
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:32,940
Are you going to take my savings, I wonder?

4
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:39,140
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, a little saving,
a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,240
From the pointed hat, from the water basin,

9
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls toward
the Taishakuten Gate.

10
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it will end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness too.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,540
I'm a fool who only realized it
after running around everywhere.

13
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,580
Suspicion of the Chief's Hidden Talent

14
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:36,620
I did it!

15
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,940
You finally finished it?

16
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,480
I stayed up for three whole days straight.

17
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:49,560
Behold, the Portuguese ship that sailed
mainly across the Atlantic in the 15th century.

18
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,540
It's the Caravela Atlântica.

19
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:55,960
That's amazing.
It's all made of paper, right?

20
00:01:55,960 --> 00:02:02,240
Yes, apart from the rope, every part is cut out of paper.
It's the ultimate papercraft.

21
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:06,040
Wow, they sell castles like this too,
don't they?

22
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:08,680
With a sailing ship,
the curves of the whole hull are everything.

23
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,880
It's much harder than a castle.

24
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:14,460
And I'll make the missing
parts myself to add more detail.

25
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:18,080
If only you put that much
enthusiasm into your actual work.

26
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:18,700
Good morning.

27
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,160
Good morning.

28
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,960
Ryo-san.

29
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,000
Did you already take that
document to the station?

30
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,640
Document? What are you talking about?

31
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:30,180
Chief Ohara asked you yesterday, remember?

32
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:34,020
He said it was an important document, so take
it to the station right away so you don't forget.

33
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,700
Now that you mention it, that did happen.

34
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,540
You really are hopeless.

35
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:42,580
Where did you put it?

36
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:44,720
I think it was on the desk.

37
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,540
It's not there, though.

38
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:47,880
Where on earth did you lose it?

39
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,880
Wh-why is the Chief's
stamp in a place like this?

40
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,400
Th-this is the document, isn't it?

41
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,420
Here too, and here too.

42
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:03,560
Now that I think about it,
we ran out of paper while making this one,

43
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,820
so I substituted paper
that was lying nearby.

44
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,160
What are we going to do, Ryo-san?

45
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:17,360
You'd better apologize first.
He's going to blow up at some point anyway.

46
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:21,180
Damn it,
is there no way to somehow cover this up?

47
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,640
Chief. Good morning.

48
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:31,046
Morning. By the way,

49
00:03:31,096 --> 00:03:34,340
did any calls come in for me?

50
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:37,480
No, I don't think there were any.

51
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:41,140
You don't think so...
well, if there weren't any, that's fine.

52
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:53,580
You're not hiding something from me, are you?
Don't look at me like that, I'm not hiding anything.

53
00:03:55,100 --> 00:04:00,020
Your attitude is strange.
That's just your imagination, yo.

54
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,900
What are you hiding behind your back?

55
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,540
I'm not hiding anything.

56
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,480
I knew you were hiding something.

57
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,080
Come on, show me.

58
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,620
No, it's nothing.

59
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:10,340
Show me.

60
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:12,020
I told you, it's nothing.

61
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:12,640
Show it to me!

62
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:12,820
Yes?

63
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:15,260
I said there's nothing.

64
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:15,860
Show me.

65
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,100
Hello, is anyone there?

66
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:18,580
Hello?

67
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,180
It's me.

68
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:22,880
I told you not to call me here.

69
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,360
I'll call you back.

70
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,840
I just remembered something.

71
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:30,640
I'm counting on you.

72
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:37,060
We somehow managed to avoid disaster.

73
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:39,780
Hasn't the Chief been acting weird lately?

74
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,800
Now that you mention it, he has.

75
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:45,480
He seems oddly restless, too.

76
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:49,000
And he seems to be making a
lot of phone calls somewhere.

77
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:52,360
Restless and making calls?

78
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,620
Whoa! Oh my god!

79
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:56,240
Argh!

80
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,750
Gah, how terrifying.

81
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,110
I thought that kind of thing only
happened on TV and in magazines,

82
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,440
but not even the Chief, of all people.

83
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,400
W-what is it, Ryo-chan?

84
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:06,540
He's having an affair.

85
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:14,660
Surely you're overthinking it, senpai.

86
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:17,000
The Chief would never
do something like that.

87
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,720
Chief Ohara is a very serious man.

88
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,340
You know that too, Ryo-chan.

89
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:25,120
Naive, naive, so incredibly naive!

90
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,360
Take a look at this.

91
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,100
No play, just work, work, work.

92
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:33,140
The ones who seem the most
serious are the most dangerous.

93
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,840
When the kids leave home
to marry or find jobs,

94
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:39,140
it's bound to happen, isn't it?

95
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:44,760
for a man who has lived only
for work as time goes by,

96
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,820
he doesn't even have anything
to talk about with his wife.

97
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:51,320
the hole in his heart just
keeps growing day by day.

98
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,360
That's when

99
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,920
he happens to meet a
young woman just his type.

100
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:03,300
It's like the thrill of a
first love coming back to life.

101
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,720
And from there,
it's straight down the road to an affair.

102
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,160
That Chief of ours, no way...

103
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,340
No doubt about it.

104
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,460
Ryo-sama.

105
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,620
It's been a long time.

106
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:22,960
Chief is having an affair?

107
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:25,420
I can't believe it.

108
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:27,300
It's just speculation, you know.

109
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:29,640
And there's no evidence or anything.

110
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,720
But now that you mention it, the other day

111
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:37,500
I saw the Chief buying disposable
diapers at the local supermarket.

112
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,520
Looking back, that was strange, wasn't it?

113
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:42,100
Why would the Chief be buying diapers?

114
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,360
That's definitely suspicious.

115
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,160
He has a secret child!

116
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:49,300
The Chief already has a secret child!

117
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,560
No way...

118
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,020
It can't be.

119
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,420
I can't believe it.

120
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,980
I don't want to believe it either.

121
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,560
The Chief left early today, didn't he?

122
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:10,220
Yeah, I think so.

123
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:15,500
That phone call earlier must have
been his mistress summoning him.

124
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,400
There he comes.

125
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:26,660
Looks like he's heading toward the station.

126
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,620
Hey, don't cling to me so much, Marian.

127
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,680
You're still a man, after all.

128
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:34,880
It's not my hobby.

129
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:37,500
But we're disguised as Beck, right?

130
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,440
We need to act more like a couple.

131
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,380
People will find it suspicious.

132
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:44,120
Ugh, stop it, you idiot.

133
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:44,940
Hey!

134
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:46,860
Uh-oh.

135
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,780
Honestly, young people these days...

136
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:56,800
In broad daylight, in a place like this...

137
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,060
Have you no shame? Shame!

138
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:08,120
My hunch was spot on.
That was close, close. Let's go, Marian.

139
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:11,080
Lord Ryo, you're number one, lun!

140
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:18,080
I wonder if he's going straight home.

141
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:20,160
No, we can't tell yet.

142
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,420
So he didn't take the train after all.

143
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:39,680
If it's shopping, he could've just done it
at the shopping street near the police box.

144
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:42,460
Maybe he doesn't want anyone
he knows to see his face.

145
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,960
This is getting more and more suspicious.

146
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:56,780
Lord Ryo.

147
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,760
He's calling his mistress's place

148
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:06,120
Those guys from earlier

149
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:09,080
Canoodling everywhere
without a care for the place.

150
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,580
It's me.

151
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,780
I'm on my way now.

152
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,960
I'm on my way now.

153
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,360
To his mistress's house, then?

154
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,920
Gacha!

155
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,480
Guh!

156
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,560
Joe-sama!

157
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:24,428
If there were mass production...

158
00:09:24,478 --> 00:09:44,140
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuugh...

159
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:44,520
Thank you very much.

160
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:47,660
So it's finally his mistress's house.

161
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,320
That's right.

162
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:57,220
Should we pick up some cake?

163
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,580
Not again.

164
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:05,160
You two getting along so well is fine,
but right in front of the public...

165
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:10,300
Honestly,
your manners are completely lacking.

166
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:16,480
That was close. We almost got caught.

167
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,300
We were so close.

168
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,420
He went into the apartment building!

169
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:29,740
Looks like that's the mistress's apartment.

170
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:32,920
Yeah, no doubt about it. Where's the Chief?

171
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,800
There he is! Fifth floor!

172
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:47,900
Whoaaaa... that's...

173
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:51,720
We've finally got the decisive evidence!

174
00:10:54,660 --> 00:11:00,080
Keeping a young woman like that as his mistress...
unforgivable! Unforgivable!

175
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,400
Unforgivable!

176
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,280
me

177
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:05,940
me

178
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:08,800
me

179
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:28,980
I can't believe the Chief
really has a secret child.

180
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,920
It may be hard to believe,
but it's the truth.

181
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:34,920
If this gets out to the higher-ups,

182
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:37,220
what will happen to Chief Ohara?

183
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:41,620
At best he'll be put on leave,
and at worst he'll be fired.

184
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,860
Fired?

185
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,940
Surely it wouldn't go that far.

186
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:48,460
Losing his job would be the best outcome.

187
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,800
If the media gets wind of this,
the Chief will

188
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:09,400
find his wife unable to bear such a life

189
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,480
and leave home.

190
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:15,540
His mistress, too, will be unable to bear
the cold stares of society and vanish.

191
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:20,940
Having lost his position and his family,
the Chief

192
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:23,880
will face a lonely old age.

193
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,620
It's Yocchi's child.

194
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:32,220
"Thank you, Daddy."

195
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,020
Congratulations.

196
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:34,880
Thank goodness.

197
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:05,160
How pathetic. So pathetic.

198
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:08,880
Hey, Marian,
was it really a woman's apartment?

199
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:13,120
I couldn't see very well from where I was.

200
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,760
Are you doubting me?

201
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,000
There's proof, too, you know.

202
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:19,700
You can't tell anything
from a screen this small.

203
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:22,160
I won't believe it until
I see it with my own eyes.

204
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,280
That's right.

205
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:25,920
Then take a good look with your
own eyes and see for yourself.

206
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,420
I'll take you there.

207
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:34,980
So the Chief went into this place.

208
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:35,940
Yes.

209
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:39,520
It's about ten-odd minutes on
foot from the police box, right?

210
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,920
It's the perfect place for Green.

211
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,360
It's not decided yet, you know.

212
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,080
This is definitely the room.

213
00:13:58,140 --> 00:13:58,660
This is it.

214
00:13:59,160 --> 00:13:59,940
I'm opening it.

215
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:01,980
No, you can't just open it!

216
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:02,900
Yeah, you can't.

217
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:07,060
You two were the ones who said you wouldn't believe
it unless you saw it with your own eyes, Roman!

218
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,680
Chief!

219
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:12,860
Aaaaaah!

220
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,240
Eeeeeeeh!

221
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,060
Oh no, how terrible!

222
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:25,520
Aaaaah!

223
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,120
What is this? Who are you people?

224
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:28,780
No...

225
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:29,940
Well...

226
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:34,300
Getting in the way of my
search operation like this!

227
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:35,160
This...

228
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,580
Mrs. Katsuyama!

229
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,360
No!

230
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:42,980
Ryo-chan! That's totally different!

231
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,060
Well, I'm off then.

232
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,320
Bu-bu-chief!

233
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:57,680
No way!

234
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:02,040
Sorry, sorry, it was just a reflex...

235
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:05,660
Ryo-sama, you've finally...

236
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:07,660
Yo, yo.

237
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:10,840
What are you guys doing here?

238
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:13,600
We just happened to be passing by...

239
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,760
By coincidence.

240
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:17,280
This is a misunderstanding!

241
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:19,160
What are you doing here, Chief?

242
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:20,900
That's...

243
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,500
Thank goodness, he's still here.

244
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,580
The Chief's mistress has a secret child!

245
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:31,380
What?

246
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:32,760
No way...

247
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:33,500
No way!

248
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,480
And I trusted him...

249
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:38,820
Dad! If you're going out,
get diapers while you're at it!

250
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,740
Everyone!

251
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:42,920
Hiromi-san!

252
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:44,980
What!?

253
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:53,380
So, because of Hideo's work,
we moved into this apartment building.

254
00:15:53,940 --> 00:15:56,920
Hello, everyone.
Thank you for all your help the other day.

255
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:00,940
If you get any new games,
lend them to me again.

256
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:05,920
My friend Megumi Marukawa
and her only daughter, Hanako.

257
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:07,280
Nice to meet you.

258
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:10,460
So the Chief wasn't
having an affair after all?

259
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,740
Affair my foot. Cut the nonsense.

260
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:16,220
It's mostly the Chief's fault.

261
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:19,840
Hiromi moved right here into our neighborhood,
and you were hiding it from us?

262
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:23,520
Exactly, why didn't you tell us right away?

263
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:25,380
Well, that's...

264
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,380
Dad didn't want everyone teasing him,
did he, Grandpa?

265
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:34,740
Why do I have to be called "Grandpa Chief"?

266
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:37,520
Sure, I do think he's a stubborn old geezer.

267
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:40,000
Wait, could it be that...

268
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:44,080
Yes, I was just discharged
from the hospital last week.

269
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:49,100
I see. Well, congratulations.

270
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,440
Congratulations.

271
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,440
So, is it a boy or a girl?

272
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,660
It's a boy.

273
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:56,880
Is that so? Congratulations.

274
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:59,460
Chief, why didn't you tell us?

275
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,920
Were you talking about a pet or something?

276
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:03,360
A grandson.

277
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:06,300
What? I was talking about my grandson!

278
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:10,060
The Chief has a grandchild?

279
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:19,460
So cute! He looks like a little doll.

280
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,760
So his name is Daisuke? That's a good name.

281
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:27,040
We took the
"Dai" character from Ohara's name.

282
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,200
Hiromi's your only daughter, right?

283
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:33,080
So we wanted to keep Ohara's name somewhere in there,
and that's why we chose it.

284
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:37,080
Wow, he does look a bit like the Chief.

285
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:38,500
You think so?

286
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:43,320
Actually, the head doctor at the
hospital said he has my eyes, too.

287
00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:46,840
But people often say he has Hideo's mouth.

288
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,300
No, no, he's definitely more like me.

289
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,620
Hey, hey, let me see him too!

290
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,580
Sorry.

291
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:57,967
Hey, don't get within one meter of him.

292
00:17:58,017 --> 00:18:00,680
If spit flies and he gets sick,
it'll be a disaster.

293
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:04,106
Don't talk about people like they're germs.

294
00:18:04,156 --> 00:18:05,960
Let's see, what kind of face is it?

295
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:08,480
Whoa!

296
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:12,200
Hey, doesn't he look like Hideo?

297
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:13,880
He looks like me, doesn't he, Ryotsu?

298
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:16,960
If anything, he looks more like a monkey.

299
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,830
A monkey?! You...

300
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:21,480
You're calling my grandson a monkey!

301
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:24,286
You misheard, Chief. I never said monkey.

302
00:18:24,336 --> 00:18:28,200
I said he looks just like
a noble person's childhood.

303
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,480
A noble person?

304
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:35,463
Yes, that's right.
This face, overflowing with dignity.

305
00:18:35,513 --> 00:18:39,156
He's truly a aristocrat born to it,
you could say.

306
00:18:39,206 --> 00:18:42,740
This child's future is
shining with a truly rosy glow.

307
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:48,120
W-Is that so? I've thought he
has a rather dignified face, too.

308
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,720
Ryotsu, you think so too?

309
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:52,312
That's right, Hiromin,

310
00:18:52,362 --> 00:18:54,900
you know that fine sake
you brought the other day?

311
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:55,940
Bring that out for us.

312
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:57,420
Yes, yes, I'll bring it right out.

313
00:18:57,900 --> 00:19:01,140
I just said what I was thinking,
but I guess that was wrong of me.

314
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,760
Come on, do your best!

315
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,200
Didn't you definitely say "monkey" though?

316
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:09,720
As expected of you, senior,
you're so good at covering things up.

317
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:15,220
Good sake really is delicious.

318
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,740
Hiromi-san, you wouldn't happen to have
some snacks or something, would you?

319
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,600
Yes, I'm preparing something now.

320
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,760
Hey, Ryotsu, have a little restraint…

321
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:25,709
Speaking of which, I also looked
at little Daisuke's arms and legs,

322
00:19:25,759 --> 00:19:27,180
and they're really nicely built.

323
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:31,500
That's the kind of musculature that
could make him a top-class athlete.

324
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:33,883
I see. Hey, Hiromi,

325
00:19:33,933 --> 00:19:36,080
bring out something tasty, will you?

326
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:38,420
That caviar you brought the other day, or
whatever it was, we still have that, right?

327
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:40,400
Yes, yes, understood.

328
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:46,960
Mm, wow, this caviar really tastes great.

329
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:49,180
Hiromi-san, another bottle of sake.

330
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:50,240
Coming!

331
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:54,560
Daisuke's face is handsome,
and that settles it.

332
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,020
Th-thanks, I suppose.

333
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,200
Ryo-chan, it's about time we

334
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:00,920
Daisuke-kun, bazoo!

335
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:07,500
Well, well, look at you two,
completely plastered.

336
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,880
Well then,
we should be taking our leave now.

337
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,500
Senpai, let's head home.

338
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:15,900
What, you're leaving already?
We haven't even eaten yet!

339
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:19,640
So you were planning to stay for dinner too?

340
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:26,760
Right, speaking of which, Daisuke has
the same clever-looking eyes as the Chief.

341
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:31,960
Since you're here,
why don't you all stay and have dinner?

342
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:35,600
Hiromi, call the sushi shop.
Seven orders of top-grade nigiri.

343
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,460
Understood.

344
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:41,360
Chief, is that really all right?

345
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:47,480
From what I've seen, Daisuke will
definitely grow into a great man.

346
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:52,180
A birth celebration meal
for a man of such stature...

347
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:56,180
Is seven orders of top-grade
nigiri really enough?

348
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:59,140
It might go down in history, you know.

349
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,500
Well, that's true.

350
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:04,500
Hiromi, make that ten orders of top-grade.

351
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,100
No, no, twenty orders!

352
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:09,160
And don't forget the sea urchin,
salmon roe, and kimo-zu.

353
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:11,560
Grandpa, the president!

354
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,180
What a delight, truly delightful.

355
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:30,840
Thank you all so much for coming today.

356
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,700
Thank you very much.

357
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:36,660
We're the ones who should thank you,
we've been treated to such a feast.

358
00:21:36,660 --> 00:21:38,360
Thank you very much indeed.

359
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,880
I wish every day could be like this.

360
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:45,460
Yeah, yeah,
tomorrow hell is waiting for us, isn't it.

361
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:48,260
Hell? What are you talking about?

362
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:49,800
Don't tell me you forgot?

363
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,960
The reflection reports.

364
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:53,660
Reflection reports?

365
00:22:01,340 --> 00:22:02,680
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

366
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:04,860
You don't look well.

367
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,120
N-no, it's nothing.

368
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:09,440
Come on, come on, drink up, drink up.

369
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,383
So wow, no...

370
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:15,200
What a good day. What a windfall!

371
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:17,200
Hey, hahaha.

372
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:19,100
Ryotsu!

373
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,390
You... you,

374
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:28,540
You made that document into scrap paper?!

375
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:32,280
W-w-it was just a little mix-up!

376
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:35,660
A mix-up?
You're something else, you know that?

377
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:41,420
And Daisuke's eyebrows look just like yours,
Chief, those manly eyebrows!

378
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:46,780
He's sure to grow into a strong-willed,
manly man, just like you, Chief.

379
00:22:48,820 --> 00:22:50,000
R-really?

380
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:54,480
Don't try to change the subject!
We're talking about the documents right now.

381
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:59,320
Speaking of which, Daisuke's ears
are impressively full, aren't they?

382
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:03,080
He's bound to be blessed with good
fortune in money when he grows up.

383
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:05,440
He'll become a billionaire, I'm sure of it.

384
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:07,260
R-really.

385
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:10,200
I told you not to try to change the subject!

386
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:14,160
Speaking of which,
Daisuke's nose is wonderful too!

387
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:16,100
S-so that's how it is...

388
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:19,480
When do you think the
Chief's thunder will strike?

389
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:22,200
When we run out of things to praise him for.

390
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:24,720
Ryo-san...

391
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:28,520
Above all, Daisuke's round, bright eyes,

392
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:31,280
sparkling like that,
he's sure to become a star.

393
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,260
No doubt about it!

394
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:33,800
A star?

395
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:36,880
No! Daisuke's adorable little hands!

396
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:39,060
Those are golden hands
that will grasp the world!

397
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:40,220
Golden hands?

398
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:42,280
Daisuke's silky-smooth hair!

399
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,080
Ryotsu!

400
00:23:43,180 --> 00:23:45,120
Daisuke's adorable little belly button!

401
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:47,240
Hey, wait! Ryotsu!

402
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:51,120
Daisuke's, Daisuke's, adorable teeth!

403
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:53,400
He doesn't have any teeth yet!

404
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,460
Hey, give up already!

405
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:58,180
Daisuke's dimples! Daisuke's peach fuzz!

406
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:01,880
Daisuke's lips!
Daisuke's ferocious tiger brow!

407
00:24:04,840 --> 00:24:10,240
C-Chief! The Chief's precious matsutake
grove has been ravaged by thieves!

408
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:14,100
For the sake of the matsutake
and for Daisuke and Hiromi too.

409
00:24:14,100 --> 00:24:18,100
This unworthy Kankichi Ryotsu
will protect the matsutake grove!

410
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:21,900
Next time, the Matsutake Security Squad rolls out!
See you then!

411
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:37,280
They say I'm a woman who
can't fall in love, but

412
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:41,980
I have so many things I want to do.

413
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

414
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,200
I want to be freer than a bird.

415
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams that change
at the speed of a kaleidoscope.

416
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,620
me

417
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:09,880
me

418
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:11,680
me

419
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:13,680
me

420
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:20,620
me

421
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:25,060
me

422
00:25:25,060 --> 00:25:26,100
me

423
00:25:26,940 --> 00:25:27,920
me

424
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:28,320
me

425
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:35,460
me

426
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:40,880
Thank you for watching.

